tify TXNRD1 substrates and map protein-protein interactions. This supports the proposed use of TMT-based multiplexed quantification and LC-MS/MS for large-scale protein quantification, and the use of targeted tandem mass spectrometry to validate mono-ADP-ribosylation supports the proposed validation strategy of using targeted MS, biochemical assays, and western blotting to confirm predicted target engagement. However, this work was not a thermal shift assay, did not use PISA, and did not address K562 cells, native lysates, small-molecule drug screening, the 48-58C thermal window, TMTPro 16-plex design, 384 hours of instrument time, 96 compounds, 10 uM treatment for 30 minutes, or the proposed empirical cutoffs. The weakest support is that neither related work provides direct evidence for the claimed 8-fold theoretical throughput improvement of PISA over traditional TPP and CETSA methods, nor for the proposed scale of approximately 871,120 thermal stability measurements in cells and 627,176 measurements in lysates.",
